UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 24, Lesson 1: Theme and the author''s message', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Theme is the bigger idea a story explores; readers support it with events and language, not only a sticker-like moral.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same strategy to an unfamiliar topic or audience, then compare the effect of two different choices.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nSuggest a theme and one evidence event for a story where a child returns a lost purse before shopping.\n\nFEEDBACK\nTheme: honesty/doing the right thing. Evidence: returned the purse first.\n\nCHECK\nTheme is not the same as the topic (e.g. \"fog\" is topic; \"courage in uncertainty\" may be theme).","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nFor two stories, state topic vs theme, give two evidence points each and explain why one theme fits better than a shallow slogan.\n\nWrite a short reflection describing one specific revision you made and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"English","learning_intention":"Theme is the bigger idea a story explores; readers support it with events and language, not only a sticker-like moral.","lesson_number":1,"lesson_role":"Reading","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN2-RECOM-01","EN2-UARL-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: For two stories, state topic vs theme, give two evidence points each and explain why one theme fits better than a shallow slogan. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: